<title>USA: Metal Recovery says suit without merit.</title>
<headline>Metal Recovery says suit without merit.</headline>
<dateline>EAST CHICAGO, Ind. 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Metal Recovery Technologies Inc said on Monday that a lawsuit filed against the company by a shareholder is without merit and will be vigilantly contested.</p>
<p>The suit alleges the de-zincing company was involved in securities fraud.</p>
<p>The company said the shareholder first purchased shares in 1993 and has not bought shares since the company began its new de-zincing business in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;The lawsuit is completely without foundation,&quot; said Chief Executive Officer Michael Lucas in a statement.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
